**Implementation** (gently-emd): ported upstream `Node::_wrapped_label` into `crates/gently-core/src/render/ascii/labels.rs` — when the effective `textwrap` ≠ `none` (object attr → class → graph, upstream `inherit` over graph default `none`), wrapping *replaces* the 527 escape split: `\n`/`\r`/`\l`/`\c` → spaces, whitespace collapsed, breaks at the last space (dropped) or last hyphen (kept) once a line reaches the width; `auto` = `int(sqrt(bytes)·1.4)` floored at 2; all rows keep the object's default alignment. Wired through `geometry.rs` (node box widths + labelled-gap widths from the wrapped lines; `label_lines` resolves before `column_geometry` in `canvas.rs`). Layout untouched — it is label-agnostic. Split into helpers (`wrap_width`/`flatten_escapes`/`collapse_spaces`/`wrap_lines`/`wrap_point`, plus `frame_grid`/`edge_arrow_flags`/`label_cell_width`) to clear the pretender ratchets that initially blocked the commit.

